 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you doing? For most people, yes. A hundred miles is good goal. Are you training regularly? On average, people ride about ten miles per hour on flat terrain. So a hundred miles would take about ten hours. It is. You' want to plan rest stops and nutrition along the way. Increments work. A short, half hour ride on weekend can build your confidence. A mix of distance and speed work is best. Try long rides on weekends, and do couple of short, fast rides during the week.",
